      "title": "Using Dust.js at Paypal and LinkedIn",
      "description": "Jeff Harrell from PayPal talks about how he and his team at PayPalare using Dust and JavaScript templating to enable rapid, lean UX development from prototype to production, and to bridge their legacy and new UI technology stacks.\n\nFrom LinkedIn, Veena Basavarajpresents on how LinkedIn uses [3]Dust.js to render page templates, using JavaScript, on both the client and server. She will be talking about challenges and solutions for generating e-mails, site SEO, formatting / localization, and AB testing.",
